            <ArticleTitle>Coronary perforation: What color is your parachute?</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>405-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1002/ccd.26126</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Coronary perforation is a rare but devastating complication of PCI, requiring rescue devices such as covered stents. This paper documents the successful use of a pericardial covered stent in 9/9 patients for coronary perforation. Pericardial covered stents have theoretical advantages over PTFE covered stents, but clinical studies proving this are not feasible.</AbstractText>
